### =====================================================================
### JURIKA — Smoke tests Sprint 1 (Securite production)
###
### Pre-requis :
###   - Stack demarree (RS256, refresh max 5 sessions, rate limit actif, HTTPS).
###   - Cles JWT presentes dans infrastructure/secrets/jwt/.
###
### Compte demo :
###   Workspace : JUR-DEMO1
###   Email     : karim@jurika.ma
###   Password  : Admin@2026
### =====================================================================

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@auth    = http://localhost:8081

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Workspace check (sensitive route — rate limit 10/min)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name workspaceCheck
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/workspace-check
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspaceCode": "JUR-DEMO1"
}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Login (genere access RS256 + refresh)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name login
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspaceCode": "JUR-DEMO1",
  "email": "karim@jurika.ma",
  "password": "Admin@2026"
}

###
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.tokens.accessToken}}
@refreshToken = {{login.response.body.tokens.refreshToken}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Verifier que le token est bien RS256
###    (copier accessToken et le decoder sur jwt.io → header.alg == "RS256")
### -------------------------------------------------------------------

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Appel ressource protegee (verifie la cle PUBLIQUE par ticket-service)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Refresh token (rotation : ancien revoqued, nouveau emis)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
# @name refresh
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###
@newRefresh = {{refresh.response.body.refreshToken}}

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Re-utilisation ancien refresh -> 401 (rotation OK)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}
### Attendu : 401 Unauthorized

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. Limite 5 sessions actives — simuler 6 logins (RG-SAAS-12)
###    Repeter le login 6 fois ; le 1er refresh emis doit etre revoque automatiquement.
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Repeter 6x la requete (etape 2). Verifier en DB :
#   SELECT COUNT(*) FROM refresh_tokens
#   WHERE user_id = (SELECT id FROM users WHERE email='karim@jurika.ma')
#     AND revoked_at IS NULL AND expires_at > NOW();
# Attendu : 5

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. Rate limit auth sensible (10 req/min sur /login)
###    Lancer 11 fois cette requete rapidement (script PowerShell ci-dessous).
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "workspaceCode": "JUR-DEMO1",
  "email": "wrong@jurika.ma",
  "password": "wrong"
}
### Attendu : a partir de la 11eme requete -> 429 Too Many Requests
### Headers verifies : X-RateLimit-Remaining, X-RateLimit-Replenish-Rate

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 9. CORS — origine non whitelistee bloquee
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
OPTIONS {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/login
Origin: https://malicious-cabinet.com
Access-Control-Request-Method: POST
### Attendu : reponse SANS header Access-Control-Allow-Origin

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 10. HSTS / CSP / X-Frame-Options — headers presents
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/workspace-check
### Verifier les headers de reponse :
###   Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
###   X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
###   X-Frame-Options: DENY
###   Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; ...
###   Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
###   Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), microphone=(), camera=()

### -------------------------------------------------------------------
### 11. Logout (refresh revoque)
### -------------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{newRefresh}}"
}
### Attendu : 204 No Content

### Puis verifier que le refresh est inutilisable
POST {{gateway}}/api/v1/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{newRefresh}}"
}
### Attendu : 401 Unauthorized

